# TTZip Project Licensing & Intellectual Property Architecture

TTZip is architected with a tiered licensing model designed to foster open-source developer adoption across multi-language SDK ecosystems while safeguarding native desktop client applications and brand identities.

---

## 1. Core Infrastructure & Multi-Language SDKs (Permissive Dual-License)
All core compression engines, safe Rust microkernels, C-ABI bindings, and SDK distribution packages are dual-licensed under:
- **BSD 3-Clause License** (`BSD-3-Clause`)
- **Apache License, Version 2.0** (`Apache-2.0`)

You may choose either license at your option.

**Covered Subsystems:**
- `core/rust/` (`ttzip-engine`, `ttzip-glue`, `ttzip-cli`, `ttzip-tui`)
- `core/Sources/CTTZipBridge/` (C11 FFI Bridge and public C-ABI)
- `core/Sources/TTZipCore/` (Swift 6 native SDK)
- `core/sdk/` (Python, Java Panama FFM, Go CGO, Node.js / TypeScript SDKs)
- `homebrew/` (Official Homebrew packaging Formula)

---

## 2. Native Client Applications (Copyleft GPLv3 License)
All end-user GUI applications, system QuickLook previews, and FinderSync context integration extensions are licensed under:
- **GNU General Public License Version 3 or later** (`GPL-3.0-or-later`)

**Covered Subsystems:**
- `apple/Sources/TTZipApp/` / `core/Sources/TTZipApp/` (macOS native desktop GUI application)
- `apple/Sources/TTZipFinderSync/` / `core/Sources/TTZipFinderSync/` (Finder extension)
- `apple/Sources/TTZipQuickLook/` / `core/Sources/TTZipQuickLook/` (QuickLook preview plugin)

---

## 3. Third-Party & Upstream Open-Source Foundations
Embedded third-party libraries and upstream contribution patches (e.g. libarchive, Zstandard, XZ Utils, libdeflate, LZ4) are licensed under their respective upstream permissive licenses (BSD-2-Clause, MIT, 0BSD, Public Domain). See `core/ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS.md` and individual vendor directory licenses.

---

## 4. Trademark & Commercial Licensing
"TTZip", official logos, and application trade dress are protected marks of Witt Kung. For commercial closed-source GUI embedding or enterprise licensing, contact `witt.w.kung@gmail.com`.
